Ata uses, at runtime, the following third-party software and models.

whisper.cpp — MIT licence
  https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
  Built from source and bundled inside Ata.app as whisper-cli.

OpenAI Whisper models (ggml conversions) — MIT licence
  https://github.com/openai/whisper
  https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
  Downloaded on first use; not bundled.

Silero VAD — MIT licence
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  Downloaded on first use; not bundled.

LAME 3.100 (the MP3 encoder) — GNU LGPL, version 2 or later
  https://lame.sourceforge.io
  Built into Ata from source in Sources/CLame, where the licence (COPYING) and the
  exact files taken are listed. Ata's full source is public, so it can be rebuilt
  against a modified LAME. LAME is offered under version 2 of the LGPL "or any
  later version"; Ata relies on that option and takes it under version 3, which is
  compatible with the Apache License 2.0.

FluidAudio — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio
  Compiled into Ata.

Speaker diarization models, Core ML conversions by FluidInference — CC BY 4.0
  https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/speaker-diarization-coreml
  Includes pyannote segmentation and WeSpeaker speaker-embedding models.
  pyannote: https://github.com/pyannote/pyannote-audio (MIT)
  WeSpeaker: https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wespeaker
  Downloaded on first use of voice recognition; not bundled.
  Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
